SUMMARY:Feast of Osia Methodia\, Chorio
LOCATION:Chorio\, Kimolos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Kimolos's own saint\, Osia Methodia (1861–1908)\, is honoured at the Panagia Odigitria church where her relics rest: vespers on 4 October\, liturgy and a procession of the relics on the 5th\, then a glenti with live folk music laid on by the residents and the municipality. It is an off-season feast\, so ferries are thin — come from Milos by the Pollonia boat and stay the night.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kimolos/#chorio-feast-of-osia-methodia-chorio
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kimolos/#chorio-feast-of-osia-methodia-chorio
